--- bytes -- byte-buffer primitives for the `Bytes` scalar type.
---
--- Single source of truth for the `bytes` stdlib interface: 8 functions
--- covering construction from lists of ints, projection back to lists,
--- concatenation, slicing, length, indexing, and UTF-8 coding. `Bytes` is
--- the contiguous byte-buffer value type declared in `value_types.yaml`
--- (ADR-0083 §2.1, encoded on the JSON boundary as `{"__bytes__": [n,
--- ...]}`); before this module the only producer was the FFI `out_buf`
--- descriptor, so `.hnl` code had no way to build or inspect one.
---
--- All 8 functions are FFI atoms: `Bytes` has no literal syntax and no
--- eval-vocabulary constructor, so construction, indexing, slicing, and
--- UTF-8 coding cannot be expressed as pure handl arrows. The
--- `op`/`handl` declaration form (ADR-0077 Phase 2) declares the
--- interface; the Rust `Function` impls in
--- `plugin-lib-stdlib::ops::bytes` provide the logic and are registered
--- in an `OpRegistry` that dispatches each `op` to its native impl.
---
--- `bytes.slice(b, offset, len)` clamps the window to the buffer (like
--- `str.slice`); `bytes.at(b, i)` errors when `i` is out of bounds (like
--- `str.char_at`); `bytes.utf8_decode` errors on invalid UTF-8.
---
--- ## Capability declarations (ADR-0077 Phase 4)
--- bytes.from_list -- build a Bytes buffer from a list of ints (each must be 0..=255).
--- bytes.to_list -- project a Bytes buffer to a list of ints.
--- bytes.concat -- concatenate two Bytes buffers.
--- bytes.slice -- copy out the `len`-byte window at `offset`, clamped to the buffer.
--- bytes.len -- byte length of a Bytes buffer.
--- bytes.at -- the byte at `index` (error when out of bounds).
--- bytes.utf8_encode -- UTF-8 encode a String into Bytes.
--- bytes.utf8_decode -- UTF-8 decode Bytes into a String (error on invalid UTF-8).
cap "bytes.from_list"
cap "bytes.to_list"
cap "bytes.concat"
cap "bytes.slice"
cap "bytes.len"
cap "bytes.at"
cap "bytes.utf8_encode"
cap "bytes.utf8_decode"
op "bytes.from_list" : (List Int) -> Bytes
  guarantee: True
op "bytes.to_list" : Bytes -> (List Int)
  guarantee: True
op "bytes.concat" : (Bytes * Bytes) -> Bytes
  guarantee: True
op "bytes.slice" : (Bytes * Int * Int) -> Bytes
  guarantee: True
op "bytes.len" : Bytes -> Int
  guarantee: True
op "bytes.at" : (Bytes * Int) -> Int
  guarantee: True
op "bytes.utf8_encode" : String -> Bytes
  guarantee: True
op "bytes.utf8_decode" : Bytes -> String
  guarantee: True
handle "bytes.from_list" with rust_bytes_from_list
handle "bytes.to_list" with rust_bytes_to_list
handle "bytes.concat" with rust_bytes_concat
handle "bytes.slice" with rust_bytes_slice
handle "bytes.len" with rust_bytes_len
handle "bytes.at" with rust_bytes_at
handle "bytes.utf8_encode" with rust_bytes_utf8_encode
handle "bytes.utf8_decode" with rust_bytes_utf8_decode
